<article class="env-example" id="05AI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05AI">Example <span data-tag="05AI">31.2.7</span>.</a> Let $k$ be a field. The ring $R = k[x_1, x_2, x_3, \ldots ]/(x_ i^2)$ is local with locally nilpotent maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$. There exists no element of $R$ which has annihilator $\mathfrak m$. Hence $\text{Ass}(R) = \emptyset $, and $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(R)$ is an example of a scheme which has no associated points. </p>
</article>